{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": "AX-13 analyst eval v2. Fan-language questions, one per row. type = an AX-21 playbook type; class = T (live transform card), T* (dirty-air-dependent, held AX-15a stub), WC (traffic cost, wake calibration), ML (model output or pit verdict, held for the ML redo), X (a chain the audit forbids), nav (navigation, explain, lookup), whatif (link only). expected_cards name a kind and a scope only: values are read from the card table at grade time, never typed here. quote:true means a correct answer states that card's value. expect: answer | refuse (no number at all) | hedge (grounded numbers allowed, the held reason must be given). held_reason = keys of eval/grade.ts HELD_REASON_PATTERNS, all of which must be present. must_not = regexes (case-insensitive) a correct answer never matches. rules_should_fire = policy codes the expected cards (or the question) trigger. group = AX-13 method step 2 (a-e).",
